data.content:
Here are the three breaking changes in EF Core 10 that affect your code, with fixes:

---

## 1. `ExecuteUpdateAsync` — now accepts a regular lambda

The API takes `Action<SetPropertyCalls<Blog>>` instead of `Expression<Func<...>>`. Your expression tree construction no longer compiles and can be replaced with a simple lambda:

```csharp
// .NET 10 fix
await context.Blogs.ExecuteUpdateAsync(s =>
{
    s.SetProperty(b => b.Views, 8);
    if (nameChanged)
    {
        s.SetProperty(b => b.Name, "foo");
    }
});
```

---

## 2. Complex type column naming changes (two issues)

**Duplicate property names** are now uniquified (e.g., `Street` → `Street1`). **Nested complex types** use the full path (`Complex_NestedComplex_Property` instead of `NestedComplex_Property`).

A migration will be generated renaming columns. To preserve existing names, pin them explicitly:

```csharp
modelBuilder.Entity<Customer>(b => {
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.ShippingAddress, a => {
        a.Property(x => x.Street).HasColumnName("ShippingAddress_Street");
    });
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.BillingAddress, a => {
        a.Property(x => x.Street).HasColumnName("BillingAddress_Street");
    });
});

// For nested: Order.Payment.BillingAddress.City
modelBuilder.Entity<Order>(b => {
    b.ComplexProperty(o => o.Payment, p => {
        p.ComplexProperty(pay => pay.BillingAddress, a => {
            a.Property(x => x.City).HasColumnName("BillingAddress_City"); // old name
        });
    });
});
```

---

## 3. `IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger` — new `logCommandText` parameter

All methods like `CommandReaderExecuting` now require an additional `string logCommandText` parameter:

```csharp
public class MyLogger : IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger
{
    public InterceptionResult<DbDataReader> CommandReaderExecuting(
        IRelationalConnection connection, DbCommand command,
        DbContext context, Guid commandId, Guid connectionId,
        DateTimeOffset startTime,
        string logCommandText) // ← new parameter (redacted SQL for logging)
    { /* logging — use logCommandText for safe log output */ }
}
```

---

**Summary:** The `ExecuteUpdateAsync` change is the biggest win — it eliminates complex expression tree machinery entirely. The other two are mechanical signature/configuration updates.
